---
description: |
  Deduplicates HarfangLab Module Activity (`class_uid` 1005) per window, host,
  module, and loading process. Events of other classes pass through
  unchanged.

  The first load of every module by a process executable in a window passes
  through immediately and unchanged, with the process ID and the base
  address. Further loads of the module by the same executable in the same
  window are repeats: when the window closes, one summary event stands for
  them, and a key without repeats gets no summary. A summary is a Module
  Activity event with the OCSF aggregation attributes: `count` holds the
  number of repeats, which excludes the first load, `start_time` and
  `end_time` the times of the first and last repeat, `duration` the time
  between them, and `time` equals `start_time`. All times are epoch
  milliseconds, like HarfangLab's. Only summaries have `count`.

  The key covers the whole module file record, with its path, size, hashes,
  and signature, so another binary at the same path gets its own summary,
  and the load type. It also covers the loading process by its executable
  path and name (`actor.process.file.path`, `actor.process.name`), so a
  module that an unusual process loads gets a first occurrence of its own.
  The base address differs between loads and doesn't appear in a summary.
  The process ID of the loading process appears only if all repeats came
  from the same one.

  The summary takes the device and the metadata from the first event of the
  host with the same activity and severity in the window.

  Windows close on the wall clock every `window`, and every summary covers at
  most one `window` of event time. The package description explains the
  windowing, the memory it needs, and how a SIEM counts summaries.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 1h
      description: Width of the deduplication windows, in processing and event
        time.
---

// `$window` names the argument only outside the `window` block.
if class_uid == 1005 {
  _host = device?.agent_list?[0]?.uid? else device?.hostname?
  _bucket = from_epoch(time? * 1ms).floor($window)
  // Every group key and aggregate costs memory per summary. The summaries
  // therefore group by digests: `_ids` covers the values that few events of
  // a host share, and `_module` the module, which is the same on many
  // hosts. The values behind the digests come from one context record per
  // host and `_ids` and one record per `_module`. The device and metadata
  // belong to the host and come from the first event of the context.
  _ids = hash_xxh3([device?.hostname?, activity_id?, activity_name?,
    severity_id?, severity?, type_uid?, actor?.process?.file?.type_id?])
  _module = hash_md5([module?.file?, module?.load_type_id?,
    module?.load_type?, module?.type?, module?.function_name?])
  window size=$window {
    // The digest covers the same keys as the summary below. Keep both lists
    // identical, so that every summary belongs to one first occurrence.
    _key = hash_md5([_host, _bucket, _ids, _module,
      actor?.process?.file?.path?, actor?.process?.name?])
    summarize _key, _seen=count(), options={mode: "cumulative"}
    if _seen == 1 {
      drop _key, _host, _bucket, _ids, _module, _seen
    } else {
      fork_merge {
        summarize _host, _bucket, _ids, _module,
          actor?.process?.file?.path?, actor?.process?.name?,
          count=count(), start_time=min(time?), end_time=max(time?),
          _pid_min=min(actor?.process?.pid?),
          _pid_max=max(actor?.process?.pid?),
          _pid_count=count(actor?.process?.pid?)
      }, {
        summarize _host, _ids, _context=first({
          activity_id: activity_id?,
          activity_name: activity_name?,
          severity: severity?,
          severity_id: severity_id?,
          type_uid: type_uid?,
          metadata: metadata?,
          device: device?,
          actor_file_type_id: actor?.process?.file?.type_id?,
        })
      }, {
        summarize _module, _object=first({
          file: module?.file?,
          load_type_id: module?.load_type_id?,
          load_type: module?.load_type?,
          type: module?.type?,
          function_name: module?.function_name?,
        })
      }
      // Each context and module record sorts before the summaries that it
      // belongs to, so a running `first` hands it to each of them.
      sort _host?, _ids?, _context? == null
      summarize _host?, _ids?, _ctx=first(_context?),
        options={mode: "cumulative"}
      sort _module?, _object? == null
      summarize _module?, _mod=first(_object?), options={mode: "cumulative"}
      where _context? == null and _object? == null
      this = {
        activity_id: _ctx.activity_id,
        activity_name: _ctx.activity_name,
        category_uid: 1,
        class_uid: 1005,
        metadata: _ctx.metadata,
        severity: _ctx.severity,
        severity_id: _ctx.severity_id,
        time: start_time,
        start_time: start_time,
        end_time: end_time,
        duration: end_time - start_time,
        count: count,
        type_uid: _ctx.type_uid,
        actor: {
          process: {
            file: {
              path: actor.process.file.path,
              type_id: _ctx.actor_file_type_id,
            },
            name: actor.process.name,
            pid: _pid_min
              if _pid_min == _pid_max and _pid_count == count else null,
          },
        },
        device: _ctx.device,
        module: _mod,
      }
      drop_null_fields
    }
  }
}
